Title:
From PE to Process

Type:
Blog Post

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
- Walkthrough of how Windows turns a Portable Executable (EXE/DLL) on disk into a running process image in memory.  
- Explains why “on-disk bytes” differ from “in-memory bytes” due to mapping, section alignment, zero-filled regions, import resolution (IAT), relocations, and runtime allocations/modifications.  
- Covers key PE structures (DOS/PE headers, COFF, Optional Header, section table, data directories) and the address concepts needed to navigate them (file offsets vs RVA vs VA).  
- Describes loader behaviors that affect analysis and reversing, including ASLR/base relocations and TLS callbacks executing before the nominal entry point.  
- Connects PE metadata to modern mitigations (DEP, CFG, hardware-enforced stack protection) and notes how policy/code integrity can affect image loading.  
- Useful for reverse engineers, malware analysts, exploit devs, and defenders correlating static triage with debugger/memory-dump observations.

Technical Focus:
- PE headers, sections, data directories (IAT, reloc, TLS, load config)
- File offset vs RVA vs VA translation and section alignment
- Windows loader behavior: image mapping, import resolution, relocation processing
- Process internals: PEB/TEB, module lists, memory regions
- Pre-entry execution paths: TLS callbacks, CRT startup vs `main`
- Mitigations/metadata: ASLR, DEP/NX, CFG, shadow stack, image-load policies

Use Cases:
- Validate whether memory-dump differences are normal loader effects vs tampering/unpacking
- Map disassembler addresses to raw file locations during reversing
- Identify early-executing code paths (TLS callbacks) used by packers/malware
- Triage binaries via imports/IAT and load-config metadata
- Debug loader issues and understand why modules fail to load under policy/mitigations
- Build a small lab workflow using `dumpbin` and WinDbg (`lm`, `!peb`, `!address`, `!dh`)

Keywords:
Portable Executable, PE format, DOS header, COFF header, Optional Header, section table, RVA, virtual address, file offset, Windows loader, CreateProcessW, image mapping, Import Address Table, imports, GetProcAddress, relocations, .reloc, ASLR, TLS directory, TLS callbacks, PEB, TEB, DEP, NX, CFG, load configuration, WinDbg, dumpbin, code integrity, process mitigation policy